0..74 Comment "//! A type calls a module\'s function through the module\'s name, as a value"
75..84 Comment "//! does."
85..88 Comment "//!"
89..165 Comment "//! A theory states its types as functions to `Type`, and a model calls them"
166..242 Comment "//! through the module that declares them. The printer writes such a type as"
243..307 Comment "//! that call. So the type must read back as the call it prints."
308..311 Comment "//!"
312..383 Comment "//! `Standard.unit` runs a function of no input by its bare name, as an"
384..460 Comment "//! unqualified `unit` runs. `Standard.same(Integer)` calls the function and"
461..533 Comment "//! decodes the code that the call returns. `Standard.after(Integer)(n)`"
534..607 Comment "//! applies the call\'s result to one more argument. A second list after a"
608..667 Comment "//! type family is not a call, and the lowering refuses it."
668..671 Comment "//!"
672..743 Comment "//! - see: #5213 — a type reads a qualified call and a call of a call"
